{{!-- Move-up / move-down arrows for one row of an item panel (issue #9).

      A partial rather than eight copies of the same markup: the six panels on
      the character sheet and the two on the NPC sheet all need it, and eight
      copies is eight chances for one list to keep working while another
      silently stops.

      Expects the enclosing row context to carry `id`, `panel`, `isFirst` and
      `isLast`, all stamped by markOrder().

      `data-panel`, NOT `data-group`: `data-group` already means "which
      LASTARC.itemCreationGroups key does the Add button create from", and the
      two vocabularies only look alike. The Attacks panel is derived from
      equipped weapons rather than being a creation group, and the NPC creation
      group `npc` renders into a panel called `items`. The integrity suite
      caught the collision. --}}
<span class="la-item__order">
  <button type="button" class="la-item__move" data-action="moveItem"
          data-item-id="{{this.id}}" data-panel="{{this.panel}}" data-direction="up"
          {{#if this.isFirst}}disabled{{/if}}
          aria-label="{{localize 'LASTARC.Action.MoveUp'}}"
          data-tooltip="{{localize 'LASTARC.Tooltip.MoveUp'}}">▲</button>
  <button type="button" class="la-item__move" data-action="moveItem"
          data-item-id="{{this.id}}" data-panel="{{this.panel}}" data-direction="down"
          {{#if this.isLast}}disabled{{/if}}
          aria-label="{{localize 'LASTARC.Action.MoveDown'}}"
          data-tooltip="{{localize 'LASTARC.Tooltip.MoveDown'}}">▼</button>
</span>
